# The v12 PREPARATION worker image: the managed preparation, one entrypoint on.
#
# W161230 slice2, `work/records/2026/09/finding-v12-managed-integration-execution/`.
# Every line carries the decision behind it, as W6633's, W39357's and W110935's
# recipes do, because each one is either inherited from a measured fact or is a
# deliberate departure from the image it is derived from.
#
# THE BASE IS AN EXPLICITLY SELECTED EXISTING PROVIDER IMAGE, AND IT HAS NO
# DEFAULT -- the same rule `Dockerfile.integration` states and for the same
# measured reason: `Dockerfile.claude` installs the provider runtime and the
# system trust store over a moving `apt-get` and a moving `npm install`, and
# W55361 measured that two builds of an unchanged tree differ in exactly those
# two layers. A build must name the digest the deployment has already validated
# and selected; a floating tag would let an unselected artefact become the base
# by omission. Building here produces a CANDIDATE, and selecting a digest is a
# separate deployment act this recipe cannot perform and does not claim.
ARG PROVIDER_BASE
FROM ${PROVIDER_BASE}

# THE WORKER MODULES, RE-COPIED FROM THE REVIEWED TREE ON PURPOSE. Byte
# identity with this tree becomes a property of THIS artefact rather than an
# inherited assumption about the base -- W39357's gate paid for that lesson,
# where an image asserting a file merely EXISTED passed every case after the
# adapter it was certifying had changed underneath it.
#
# `baton_worker.py` travels because this entry IS `baton_worker.main`: the
# preparation image has no serve loop of its own, and the frozen contract
# document travels with it because a module whose data was left behind is one
# that imports cleanly and fails at the first call that needs it.
#
# NOTHING FROM `baton_v12` IS COPIED IN, exactly as in the three images before
# this one. `reconciliation_task.py` is standard-library-only for that reason
# and this recipe is where that pays: there is no manager, Authority or store
# package here for it to have reached. A workload that could import the manager
# would be a manager running under a worker's name.
COPY worker/baton_worker.py /opt/baton/baton_worker.py
COPY worker/reconciliation_task.py /opt/baton/reconciliation_task.py
COPY worker/reconciliation_entry.py /opt/baton/reconciliation_entry.py
COPY worker/worker-control-1.0.schema.json \
     /opt/baton/worker-control-1.0.schema.json

# NO PROVIDER ADAPTER AND NO SOURCE PROFILES, and that is a departure from
# `Dockerfile.integration` rather than an oversight. A preparation runs a
# CONFIGURED CAUSAL SEQUENCE over content the manager already resolved: it asks
# no model, holds no credential and performs no checkout. `claude_agent.py` is
# absent because there is nothing here for it to adapt, and an image carrying a
# provider it never calls is an image whose credential surface nobody needed.

# THE SAME FIXED NON-ROOT PAIR as every other image in this campaign and as the
# adapter's `--user` restriction. Restated rather than inherited: the identity
# this container runs as is a property a reviewer should read in the recipe
# that produced it, and `read_launch`'s read-only proof depends on this process
# not being root.
USER 65532:65532

# ONE SHOT, EXEC FORM, NO SHELL IN THE PROCESS TREE. The manager stops this
# container by signalling PID 1, and PID 1 is Python. `reconciliation_entry.py`
# is the composition -- a reviewable artefact rather than a shell incantation --
# and it is one line: `baton_worker.main(agent=PreparationAgent())`.
ENTRYPOINT ["python3", "/opt/baton/reconciliation_entry.py"]

# Deterministic bytes and an explicit module path, as in the images before this
# one. `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE` is for the interpreter's OWN imports inside the
# container; this workload composes no child environments, so there is no
# `PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX` question here.
ENV PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 \
    PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 \
    PYTHONPATH=/opt/baton \
    PYTHONHASHSEED=0

# THERE IS DELIBERATELY NO `ENV ANTHROPIC_*` OF ANY KIND. This image asks no
# model, so a credential here would be one nothing in it could need -- and the
# provider resolves its credential from the environment FIRST, so a key present
# here would silently outrank a mounted slot for every container built from it.
#
# There is also no `ENV BATON_WORKER_*`: that transport was retired with no
# fallback (W26291), and this image's programs do not read those names.
#
# No `VOLUME`, no `EXPOSE`, no `HEALTHCHECK`: the launch, the input and the
# declared outputs are mounts the manager names per attempt, and this
# container's health is observed by the adapter through the engine rather than
# announced by the container.
